#: ../../../ethdebug.rst:39
msgid ""
"The compilation needs nothing but the sources. The resources are derived "
"from the analysis of the sources and the programs describe bytecode, so the "
"latter can only be produced when compiling via IR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ethdebug.rst:43
msgid "The Compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ethdebug.rst:45
msgid ""
"The compilation document identifies one run of the compiler and has an "
"``id`` derived from the sources, the ``compiler`` name and version and the "
"list of ``sources``. Every source carries its ``id``, ``path``, ``contents`` "
"and ``language``. A source ``id`` is a number unique within the compilation, "
"and all source references in the other documents refer to sources by it. "
"Source references include their type explicitly, for example ``{\"id\": 0, "
"\"type\": \"source\"}``. The compiler currently uses the same number as the "
"``id`` of the source in the Standard JSON output and in :doc:`source "
"mappings <internals/source_mappings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ethdebug.rst:52
msgid "The Resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ethdebug.rst:54
msgid ""
"The resources document carries its ``ethdebug`` stamp and two tables that "
"the programs refer to: ``types`` and ``pointers``. Compiler information and "
"sources are provided separately by ``ethdebug.compilation``. Both tables "
"cover all contracts of the compilation."
msgstr ""

